WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.400
The world is...

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.180
Hey! What have you done?

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.040
The world is... The world is closing,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.040
by my magic.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.760
We're getting out of here!

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.740
It's no use... Everyone...

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.220
But...

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.600
Syaoran-kun!
Don't let go of Sakura-chan and Mokona!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.040
What are you planning to do?

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.310
Get out of here.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:18.860
What happened?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.970
My magic... It's not enough.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:29.520
<b>Syaoran.</b>

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:30.880
Mokona.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.360
<b>Take off Mokona's earing.</b>

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.740
<b>Just now, the other Mokona told me
to do so through a dream.</b>

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.670
<b>Please.</b>

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.010
Damn it.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.350
Go.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:48.680
<b>Tsubasa Chronicle</b>

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:48.680
<b>Shunraiki</b>

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:51.750
Oboete iru hi no hikari de

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.920
kotori no you ni mezameta hi wo

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:07.720
Mirai nante atarimae ni kuru mono da to omotte ita

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:18.530
Suki na hito to zutto issho ni itai sonna tanjun na yume wo

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:29.290
kanaerarezu ni bokura wa koko de hanarete shimau no

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:38.960
Hayaku ichiban taisetsu na hito no tokoro e

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:49.470
kono mama kimi wo hontou ni ushinau sono mae ni

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:54.730
Kotae wa tokku ni kimatte'ru

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:03.780
Omoi wo katachi ni kaerunda

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.140
Where am I?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.500
Where are the others?

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.220
This place is Nihon Country.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.110
Tomoyo-Hime... right?

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.840
Welcome home, Kurogane.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:47.070
The voice back then...

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.530
Was me.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:50.990
<i>Go.</i>

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.740
<i>If you wish to go together.
If you wish for it from the bottom of your heart.</i>

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.340
<i>Then you have to give up something
that has the same magic power as him.</i>

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:05.830
<i>At that time,</i>

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.500
<i>the wound that my talisman couldn't protect you from,</i>

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.920
<i>brought you very close to death.</i>

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.030
<i>Even before their death, people still dream.</i>

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:21.540
Through the dream,
you told me a way to get him out?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:26.140
That technique uses
the one performing it as it's core.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:31.510
That is why. Once it is closed,
the person who used the technique can't get out of the circle.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:38.400
But in order to let you people escape,
he used up all the strength he had left.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.940
So my arm that he cast a spell on
could be switched for his body.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.860
Have you understood the meaning of true strength?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.650
Who knows.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.760
But I did get weaker...

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.600
After I killed someone.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:22.120
Did you know about that from the dream?
That this would happen if I killed him.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.200
I kept wishing that it wouldn't come this way.

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.040
<i>So is that why
you told me that this was a curse?</i>

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.780
You're not going to say: "You should have told me earlier?"

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.810
The pain of knowing and not being able to tell.
People who aren't aware of that won't understand it.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.390
Blaming those who do understand it won't help either.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.030
Kurogane.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:58.950
Besides, I don't regret losing my arm at that time.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.770
<i>I have always desired power.</i>

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.640
So that people important to me
won't be taken away by anyone.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:14.050
However, having power can also bring about chaos.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:19.160
And there are also things
strength alone cannot protect.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:31.540
The meaning of true strength.
It seems you finally understand it.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.890
Sorry to have made you wait.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.830
Please come inside.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:07:59.200
Hey?!

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.080
I've returned the favor. Kuro-sama.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.070
I'll kick your ass, you bastard!

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.080
I shall grant that wish.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.540
Don't disappear.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:54.960
Don't disappear.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.450
My other...

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.810
<b>Syaoran!</b>

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.630
<b>Good morning! Good morning!</b>

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.290
<b>Are you alright?</b>

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.170
<b>You're not hurt anymore, are you?</b>

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.020
Yeah, I'm alright now.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.900
<b>How's Sakura?</b>

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.200
This is...

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.180
<b>Sakura.</b>

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:20.620
I took the liberty of tendling her body wounds.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.990
<b>Thank you, Tomoyo.
But why is she on top of this tree?</b>

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.910
This is a sacred tree.
The oldest in all of Nihon Country.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:34.970
This sakura tree should be able to infuse
this soulless body with a little vitality.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.950
It's the same name isn't it?

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.220
Sakura.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:46.760
It seems you have returned, Kurogane.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:47.440
Yes.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.030
Still talking so rudely to Amaterasu-sama.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.150
It seems that you
have grown a little on your journey.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.360
I welcome the guest that you have brought,
you may rest here for a while.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:03.280
Though, your journey is far from over.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.930
We do have one other guest.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.260
<b>Fuuma!</b>

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:22.040
It's been a while.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:27.980
Well then again, I don't know how long it's been
for you guys since time flows differently between worlds.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:31.470
Are you looking for something here in Nihon?

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:33.960
On the contrary, I came to deliver something.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.830
What is that thing?

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.410
An artificial arm.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:46.310
There wasn't time to cover the skin
so I apologize for it's appearance.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.740
Still, I think you'll find it useful.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.050
And why did you bring that here?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:56.610
Moreover, how do you know about that?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.880
Because I asked Yuuko-san.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.460
<b>Yuuko?</b>

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:03.600
I do both things, searching and delivering.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:09.560
I got this thing from a more technologically
advanced world than this one.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.510
A Country called Piffle.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:22.650
And the price?

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:25.410
Already got them from Yuuko-san.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.810
And Yuuki-san...

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:35.480
I promised the witch
that I would pay the price while you were sleeping.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.430
<b>Fay's eye color...</b>

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:05.160
The source of my magic
are the blue colors of my eyes.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:14.520
Mokona, send this to the witch.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:15.820
<b>But...</b>

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.080
It's all right.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.090
I can still see perfectly.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:22.050
This is just the
last remaining remnant of my magic.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.920
<b>You can't! If you don't have magic...</b>

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:25.510
<b>Fay...</b>

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.220
I won't die.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.980
I still have the blood of a
vampire inside me to keep me alive.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:36.190
I won't hand over my life in exchange for something else.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.150
Not any more.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.520
<b>Okay, I'll bring it to Yuuko then.</b>

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:57.670
Mekyo!

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.340
I have received it.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.320
And the other price as well.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.420
Not bad.

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.530
Looks even better than before.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:18.370
Shut up!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:42.960
<b>Seishirou!</b>

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.830
"It's been a while" is what would I like to say.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:56.860
But I don't know how long it's been for you guys
since time flows differently between worlds.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.770
He said the same thing Fuuma said.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.590
Is it because you're brothers?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.990
It's a bit complicated.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.970
You haven't changed a bit. Seishirou-nii-san.

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.030
Neither have you, Fuuma.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:18.430
But I can't say the same thing for you guys.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.880
You guys changed quite a bit...

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:22.480
In many ways.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.480
You seem to have lost your magical power
but acquired a new power in it's place.

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:30.490
The blood of a vampire.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:35.570
<b>Fay!</b>

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.400
I presume it is Kamui's blood, isn't it?

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.510
And if it is?

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.980
Where are Kamui and Subaru?

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.950
Is that your brother?

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:07.350
Yes. Quite a nuisance, isn't he?

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:09.100
Just like my sister.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:11.980
What do you mean by that?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.740
Um... Amaterasu-sama...

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:16.810
Tomoyo-hime.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.270
You think that's the way to act
when you're asking someone a question?

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.350
You should tell him.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.000
Shut up!

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.720
Absolutely.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:25.650
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.940
I said shut up!

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:32.170
How rude of me. Then let me try again.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:35.990
You would have appear to have met the vampire twins.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.430
In another world called Tokyo.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:49.590
Are those two still in Tokyo?

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:54.390
Nope, those two left
after these guys moved on with their journey.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.040
Where?

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:58.520
Do you really think they would tell that to your little brother.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:02.490
It is said that hunters are naturally drawn to their prey.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:06.340
But it seems the ones I wish to find continue to elude me.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.670
Well then, time to move on to the next world.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:20.790
Wait!

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.630
You're also called Syaoran-kun, yes?

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.090
Where is the feather?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.630
I have it right here.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.510
Give it back.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:42.020
Back in Outo Country, which actually
turned out to be Edonis Country.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:47.030
I obtained the feather there and left something of a hurry.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:51.020
But it has the power to turn a entire fictional world into reality.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:55.490
Do you really think I can simply hand
it over just because I was told to.

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.210
Give it back.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:11.270
I suppose we can't just talk this over.

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.600
Because I have always been watching,
of what kind of person you really are.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:18.070
Through your link with your other self, yes?

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.880
That aspect of you is really like your father's.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:36.370
Though maybe because you truly are your father's son.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.140
Well then...

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.630
Please wait.

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:49.850
If you begin fighting like this,
then the Shirasagi Castle would be damaged.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.590
This is...

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.720
A Kekkai.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.090
A serperate dimesnion...

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.650
Yes, one would call this a Kekkai.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:25.410
With this, we can do whatever we want
and it will have no effect on reality.

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:29.890
Wounds, on the other hand, are as real as in the real world.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:33.680
Well then, shall we begin?

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.770
Where am I?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:01.160
Sakura-chan.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.740
Do you know me?

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:07.240
Well we did meet at Yuuko-san's shop.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:10.610
But you were sleeping at that time.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:14.730
Are we inside the shop?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.510
No, we're not.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:19.550
But this is a dream.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:21.300
A dream?

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:28.390
I'm trapped inside a dream.

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:52.990
Shall we find out the outcome of their
battle from Kurogane and Onee-sama?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.680
There is something you wish to discuss with me, right?

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:04.680
I was told that you are a dreamseer.
That you can see the future in your dreams.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.600
But when I came To Nihon Country
and met you in person.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.310
Hurry... He is going to die...

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:20.200
If he dies... If he dies...

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:22.450
It's going to be alright.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.410
Kurogane will not die.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:34.260
<i>I couldn't sense the power of a dreamseer from you.</i>

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.470
I'm the same as you.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:42.130
I gave it to that woman as a price.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:48.320
So you paid the price for us to travel here after Celes.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:55.090
We, who see the future, can do nothing
but read what lies ahead.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:21:00.630
That is why, even just a little bit we always pray
that those we love may walk a path of happiness.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:04.260
Although, there is very little that we can actually do.

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:07.690
Just like your king.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.120
So you knew Ashura-ou.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:22.560
Your king saw what was to come and searched endlessly
for a path in which you could be saved.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.230
Even as he himself started to break down.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:35.870
But to change the future is very difficult.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:41.540
Even the smallest word, the tiniest motion and the heart.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:45.820
The future takes all these as it's cues
to determinate the path ahead.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:51.040
Just like ripples on the water's surface.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:22:00.460
Because Sakura-hime knew this.
She was unable to tell anyone what she had to do.

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:07.930
When I think back to his majesty's actions,
there were many things which were hard to understand.

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:09.890
So that must have been...

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:13.850
That logic, that refusal is crumbling away.

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:17.050
For the sake of Fei Wong Reed's dream.

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:24.400
No. To destroy that logic is his wish.

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:29.030
Yes. His wish is a wish that everyone desires.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:34.250
But that logic is something that nobody can break.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:37.980
That wish is the same as mine, isn't it?

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:42.420
To bring back one who has died.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:00.980
<b><i>Syaoran!</i></b>

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:03.190
<b><i>Syaoran! Syaoran! Syaoran!</i></b>

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.000
<b>Syaoran!</b>

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:06.650
It's dangerous.

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:09.110
<b>But! But! Syaoran is going to...</b>

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:20.250
Well then, it's time to go.

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:24.820
Wait!

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:30.430
I'm not done yet.

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:34.640
So it seems.

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:39.720
Whatever it takes, I will get the feather back.

00:23:41.540 --> 00:23:44.690
<i>Raitei Shourai!</i>

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:00.550
<b>That's Sakura's feather.</b>

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:05.000
That attack just now could've been a bit dangerous.

00:24:08.420 --> 00:24:09.820
Give it back!

00:24:41.870 --> 00:24:42.540
Kid!

00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:43.960
Syaoran-kun!

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.360
<b>Syaoran!</b>

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:47.880
I'll come back together with Sakura.

00:25:06.970 --> 00:25:09.300
Could you tell me your name?

00:25:09.910 --> 00:25:12.240
Watanuki Kimihiro.

00:25:12.540 --> 00:25:16.200
That's the birthday of me and Syaoran-kun's.

00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:25.850
Sakura-chan!

00:26:15.610 --> 00:26:21.620
Kaze no naka de kimi ga naite'ru no

00:26:21.700 --> 00:26:27.750
furimukeba mou kikoenaku naru

00:26:27.830 --> 00:26:34.050
Utsutsu na no ka maboroshi na no ka

00:26:34.130 --> 00:26:40.680
Yuganda toki wo boku wa samayou

00:26:40.760 --> 00:26:46.890
Doko e itta no?
Ano koro no keshiki

00:26:46.980 --> 00:26:53.150
Komorebi no sasu
seseragi de asonde'ta

00:26:53.230 --> 00:27:00.110
Futari no koe wa
mori ni tojikomerarete

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:05.620
natsu no mukou ni kakurete'ru

00:27:05.700 --> 00:27:11.750
Toozakaru kimi no yobigoe

00:27:11.830 --> 00:27:18.050
yamanai kaze no sukima wo fukinukete

00:27:18.130 --> 00:27:24.220
